<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-09T02:25:21.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-702d84ea-bc3d-43b4-af45-a88f21996de1",
        "text": "Just like a house needs a blueprint, every webpage needs a proper structure. The very first line in an HTML document tells the browser what kind of document it is.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/7e050bbd26ff1405fc3ff06b57d13753-intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-panel-1-6d7b3f87-1f23-4c05-b35e-928b1823129e.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-37c83782-b622-466a-bee5-8fd358c98b13",
        "text": "This special declaration is `<!DOCTYPE html>`. After that, all the content and other tags for your webpage will be nested inside the main `<html>` tag, which acts as the root.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/f7c47db735dd56b946f7802da17d3747-intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-panel-2-1cf80605-69b3-4053-97c9-2a5b75975dcc.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-10c7ee10-4c46-423d-9029-600d8976391d",
        "text": "Inside the `<html>` tag, there are two major sections: the `<head>` and the `<body>`. The `<head>` section is like the brain of your page.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/a90d652eb3a4ad7ccfe24bbe48ca6eb7-intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-panel-3-47334f38-2cc9-4327-8140-39e22faee578.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-e926c405-dcfd-4f6b-ad44-6c674951b0c6",
        "text": "The `<head>` contains important information *about* the page, like its title or links to stylesheets, but none of this content is directly visible on the page itself.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/bab02312f002a46f03dbf3152ac5ab4d-intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-panel-4-f1999b71-d565-43c6-8a1c-87152df81b84.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-536b9b78-3f4c-435f-aa76-1f8212436550",
        "text": "The `<body>` section is where all the visible content of your webpage lives. Everything you see—text, images, videos—is placed inside the `<body>` tags.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/3497b1216baad537423ed0d79d23f75f-intro-lesson-1-html-document-structure-panel-5-c6a65064-cc83-474c-a050-a2f93241a6c2.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Explain the fundamental structure of an HTML document, focusing on the `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags and their respective purposes."
  },
